                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3bce782e-7128-380c-afeb-24208286c57c",
                        "entry_id": "97131710-4f7a-3862-af1f-1da366e35962",
                        "glosses": [
                            "to wink (to blink with only one eye as a message, signal, or suggestion)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9790cd45-b042-4ac6-99f6-b22efe20b8c3",
                                "sense_id": "3bce782e-7128-380c-afeb-24208286c57c",
                                "text": "— Дава́й, Глушко́в, беги́ пе́рвый.\n— Что вы, ра́зве мо́жно, тут сна́йпер у них, — сказа́л Глушко́в.\nПеребега́ть пе́рвым опа́сное ме́сто счита́лось привиле́гией нача́льников, не́мцы обы́чно не успева́ли откры́ть ого́нь по пе́рвому бегу́щему.\nБерёзкин огляну́лся на неме́цкие дома́, подмигну́л Глушкову и побежал.",
                                "translation": "'You go first, Glushkov.'\n'What do you mean? There's sure to be a sniper.'\nIt was a superior's privilege to be the first to cross a dangerous spot; usually the Germans were too slow to open fire straight away.\nByerozkin glanced round at the houses occupied by the Germans, winked at Glushkov and ran.",
                                "english": "'You go first, Glushkov.'\n'What do you mean? There's sure to be a sniper.'\nIt was a superior's privilege to be the first to cross a dangerous spot; usually the Germans were too slow to open fire straight away.\nByerozkin glanced round at the houses occupied by the Germans, winked at Glushkov and ran."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
